 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How you? The secret is layers. Start with a light foundation shade, then add several thin layers of different colors, building up the depth. Yes, a green based one. Avoid yellow or orange, they make your skin look worse. Use the same process, but mix shades accordingly. For very fair skin, add more white or light shade of brown. No, that causes uneven mixing. Blend each layer into the last with a few dabs, not brush strokes. That's often the eyeliner. Blend it lightly around the edges, then do the same with the lipstick.",
